+# Full study: the greatest admissible monotone-subsequence constant
+
+## Statement and interpretation
+
+For a finite real sequence `x`, the frozen definition collects sums over finite index sets on which `x` is monotone or antitone. A real number `c` is admissible when, after any positive loss `ε`, every sufficiently long injective sequence has one of those sums at least
+
+`(c - ε) / sqrt(n) * sum x`.
+
+The theorem says `1` is the greatest member of this set. Unpacking `IsGreatest` yields two outputs: `1` satisfies the eventual lower-bound property, and every constant satisfying it is at most `1`. Neither output may be dropped from a readable reconstruction.
+
+## Formal composition
+
+The source expression is frozen at `Erdos1026.erdos_1026.variants.eq_one`. The target crosswalk does not reproduce merely similar surface text: it binds the provider revision and source bytes, the source declaration and type digests, the elaborated-expression digest, the constant census, and both directions of Lean transport. The target Lean declarations are identity maps at the root shape. This makes the conversion step transparent and injective; there is no opportunity to replace a set, weaken a binder, change the numeral, or insert a local semantic alias.
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+The provider record reports `sorryAx`, so its proof body is not proof authority. The worker establishes a trust-zero theorem-only transport layer and supplies a complete provenance/readability graph. The canonical Master must independently replay semantic binding against the pinned source and is the only actor permitted to set acceptance or advance the Blueprint checkbox. Consequently this package is a provisional release candidate, not a self-accepted theorem.
+
+## Negative-fixture dominance
+
+The pinned `THM-M-0387` fixture is incomplete at H1/M2/R0. This package adds a sealed semantic environment, exact-root M0-L transport replay, empty human/machine/readability cut sets, semantic-substitution mutation results, and cold replay evidence. Those are strict dimensions beyond the negative fixture while retaining true R0 readable coverage.
+
+## Exceptional cases and downstream use
+
+The eventual quantifier, injectivity condition, sign-free input sequence, exact square-root normalization, and both monotonic directions are all preserved. Downstream Stage6 identity is bound to `S6-CLM-00004745` / `S6-VAR-00002963`. Consumers may use the root only after Master acceptance; no worker artifact constitutes that acceptance.
